"""Loads and validates this service's configuration, and is the ONLY package
in this service that may read an environment variable.

That rule is what makes `make config` able to print the effective
configuration truthfully. One `os.environ` lookup somewhere else and the
printed configuration is no longer the configuration the service is running
on.

Belongs here: the settings model, its defaults, YAML loading, environment
overlay, validation at startup, and the masked rendering used by
`make config`.

Does NOT belong here: anything that *uses* a config value. Configuration is
read once at startup and passed down as arguments; modules do not reach back
up for it, and there is no module-level singleton to import.

Precedence is environment variables over YAML, with deliberately no third
source. See `docs/config.md`.

Empty until Mint chunk 03. Until then the listen address is baked into
`__main__.py`, which is exactly the drift this package exists to end.
"""
